# App Strings

## Rule
- **All user-facing copy must come from `AppStrings`** (see `lib/core/strings/app_strings.dart`).
- Do not inline literal strings in widgets, dialogs, snackbars, buttons, tooltips, or error messages.

## Why
- Centralizes copy for consistency and easy review.
- Enables future localization without invasive refactors.

## Guidelines
- Keep names descriptive and product-oriented (e.g. `AppStrings.wordMatchTitle`).
- Prefer complete sentences and consistent casing/punctuation.
- Reuse existing strings before adding new ones; avoid near-duplicates.
- If string needs formatting, expose a helper (e.g. `scoreLabel(points)`), not string concatenation in UI.

